From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] test: remove unused x86-only sys/io.h include

The test program does not call any function or macro from sys/io.h. Its only
reference to iopl(3) is commented out. On riscv64 glibc does not provide
this x86-only header, so remove the unused include without changing any
test cases or expected results.

--- a/test/x86test.c
+++ b/test/x86test.c
@@ -43,8 +43,7 @@
 #include <getopt.h>
 #include <inttypes.h>
 #include <x86emu.h>
-#include <sys/io.h>
-
+
 typedef struct {
   x86emu_t *emu;
 } vm_t;
